#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Qiskit to implement ideas from the multiple-systems lesson."
msgstr "Paggamit ng Qiskit para ipatupad ang mga ideya mula sa aralin tungkol sa multiple systems."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation"
msgstr "Implementasyon sa Qiskit"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we took a first look at the `Statevector` and `Operator` classes in Qiskit, and used them to simulate operations and measurements on single qubits.\n"
"In this section, we'll use these classes to explore the behavior of multiple qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang aralin, unang tinuklas ang mga klase na `Statevector` at `Operator` sa Qiskit, at ginamit ang mga ito para mag-simulate ng mga operasyon at sukat sa mga single qubit.\n"
"Sa seksyong ito, gagamitin natin ang mga klaseng ito para tuklasin ang gawi ng maramihang qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start by importing the `Statevector` and `Operator` classes, as well as the square root function from `NumPy`.\n"
"Hereafter, generally speaking, we'll take care of all of our required imports first within each lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayo sa pag-import ng mga klase na `Statevector` at `Operator`, pati na rin ang square root function mula sa `NumPy`.\n"
"Sa susunod, sa pangkalahatan, uunahin nating ayusin ang lahat ng kinakailangang import sa simula ng bawat aralin.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tensor products {#tensor-products}"
msgstr "Mga tensor product {#tensor-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Statevector` class has a `tensor` method, which returns the tensor product of that `Statevector` with another, given as an argument.\n"
"The argument is interpreted as the tensor factor on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang klase na `Statevector` ay may `tensor` na method, na nagbabalik ng tensor product ng `Statevector` na iyon kasama ang isa pa, na ibinibigay bilang argumento.\n"
"Ang argumento ay itinuturing bilang tensor factor sa kanan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, below we create two state vectors representing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$, and use the `tensor` method to create a new vector, $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"Notice here that we're using the `from_label` method to define the states $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$, rather than defining them ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, sa ibaba ay gumagawa tayo ng dalawang state vector na kumakatawan sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$ at $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ at ginagamit ang `tensor` method para gumawa ng bagong vector, $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Pansinin dito na ginagamit natin ang `from_label` method para tukuyin ang mga estado na $\\vert 0\\rangle$ at $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ sa halip na tukuyin ang mga ito nang ating sarili.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ |01\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$ |01\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other allowed labels include \"+\" and \"-\" for the plus and minus states, as well as \"r\" and \"l\" (short for \"right\" and \"left\") for the states\n"
msgstr "Kasama sa ibang pinahihintulutang label ang \"+\" at \"-\" para sa plus at minus states, at \"r\" at \"l\" (maikli para sa \"right\" at \"left\") para sa mga estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, \"+\", \"-\" or \"right\" and \"left\" come from the context of quantum mechanical spin, in which a component of spin may point to the left or the right in an experiment; it is not referring to the right-most or left-most qubit in systems of multiple qubits. Here's an example of the tensor product of $\\vert {+} \\rangle$ and $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Dito, ang \"+\", \"-\" o \"right\" at \"left\" ay nagmumula sa konteksto ng quantum mechanical spin, kung saan ang bahagi ng spin ay maaaring tumuro sa kaliwa o kanan sa isang eksperimento; hindi ito tumutukoy sa pinaka-kanan o pinaka-kaliwang qubit sa mga sistema ng maramihang qubit. Narito ang isang halimbawa ng tensor product ng $\\vert {+} \\rangle$ at $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{1}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |01\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2} |10\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{1}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |01\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2} |10\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An alternative is to use the `^` operation for tensor products, which naturally gives the same results.\n"
msgstr "Isa pang alternatibo ay ang paggamit ng operasyong `^` para sa mga tensor product, na natural na nagbibigay ng parehong resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Operator` class also has a `tensor` method (as well as a `from_label` method), as we see in the following examples.\n"
msgstr "Ang klase na `Operator` ay mayroon ding `tensor` method (pati na rin ang `from_label` method), tulad ng makikita sa mga sumusunod na halimbawa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again, like in the vector case, the `^` operation is equivalent.\n"
msgstr "Muli, tulad ng sa kaso ng vector, katumbas ang operasyong `^`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compound states can be evolved using compound operations as we would expect — just like we saw for single systems in the previous lesson.\n"
"For example, the following code computes the state $(H\\otimes I)\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ for $\\vert\\phi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert {-i}\\rangle$ (which was already defined above).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga compound state ay maaaring i-evolve gamit ang mga compound na operasyon tulad ng inaasahan — katulad ng nakita natin para sa mga single system sa nakaraang aralin.\n"
"Halimbawa, kinakalkula ng sumusunod na code ang estado $(H\\otimes I)\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ para sa $\\vert\\phi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert {-i}\\rangle$ (na tinukoy na sa itaas).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2} |01\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2} |01\\rangle$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is some code that defines a $CX$ operation and calculates $CX \\vert\\psi\\rangle$ for $\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle$. To be clear, this is a $CX$ operation for which the left-hand qubit is the control and the right-hand qubit is the target. The result is the Bell state $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Narito ang ilang code na nagtatakda ng $CX$ na operasyon at kinakalkula ang $CX \\vert\\psi\\rangle$ para sa $\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle$. Para maging malinaw, ito ay isang $CX$ na operasyon kung saan ang qubit sa kaliwa ang kontrol at ang qubit sa kanan ang target. Ang resulta ay ang Bell state na $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga partial measurement {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we used the `measure` method to simulate a measurement of a quantum state vector.\n"
"This method returns two items: the simulated measurement result, and the new `Statevector` given this measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang aralin, ginamit natin ang `measure` method para mag-simulate ng sukat ng isang quantum state vector.\n"
"Ang method na ito ay nagbabalik ng dalawang bagay: ang na-simulate na resulta ng sukat, at ang bagong `Statevector` batay sa sukat na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, `measure` measures all qubits in the state vector.\n"
"We can, alternatively, provide a list of integers as an argument, which causes only those qubit indices to be measured.\n"
"To demonstrate this, the code below creates the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa default, sinusukat ng `measure` ang lahat ng qubit sa state vector.\n"
"Maaari naman tayong magbigay ng listahan ng mga integer bilang argumento, na nagiging dahilan upang ang mga qubit index na iyon lamang ang masuri.\n"
"Para ipakita ito, ang code sa ibaba ay gumagawa ng estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert w\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert 001\\rangle + \\vert 010\\rangle + \\vert 100\\rangle}{\\sqrt{3}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert w\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert 001\\rangle + \\vert 010\\rangle + \\vert 100\\rangle}{\\sqrt{3}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and measures qubit number 0, which is the rightmost qubit.\n"
"(Qiskit numbers qubits starting from 0, from right to left. We'll return to this numbering convention in the next lesson.)\n"
msgstr ""
"at sinusukat ang qubit number 0, na siyang pinakakanang qubit.\n"
"(Binibilang ng Qiskit ang mga qubit simula sa 0, mula kanan hanggang kaliwa. Babalik tayo sa convention na ito ng numbering sa susunod na aralin.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |001\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |001\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |100\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |100\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$ |100\\rangle$$\n"
